Include the expected type name in the :meth:`vUri.from_ical <icalendar.prop.uri.vUri.from_ical>` ``ValueError`` and use :func:`repr` on the offending value. The previous message read ``"Expected , got: <ical>"`` (missing the type name entirely), which made tracebacks useless when a caller passed a non-decodable bytes object or a value that contained whitespace. The new message is ``"Expected URI, got: <repr of ical>"``.
